  "surprise": "Mechanism falsified on its own registered checks: randomized training positions (sorted random subset of [0, 2T) per batch, ALiBi heads only, off at handoff) on 153-claude scored 664/621/664 on seeds 0/1/2 vs 676/700/685: exact means 650.00 vs 687.00, -37.00, paired -12/-79/-21, inside the registered -40..+35 but at its floor. Discard. Both falsifiers fired on every seed: held-out greedy after pretraining 0.658/0.785/0.836 (153: 0.9675; registered < 0.93 = in-distribution decoding damaged) and round-1 RL targets solved 396/350/452 at sample acc 0.096/0.062/0.101 (153: 766/747/694 at 0.27), so the handed-off sampler was roughly half as good on the 7+ line targets it was meant to help. Val loss at 285 s was ordinary (0.090/0.087/0.096 vs 0.088/0.087/0.089, arange positions) while greedy decoding collapsed: the model fits the stretched-position distribution, and arange positions (every gap 1) are OUT of that distribution even though every test distance is inside the trained range. Reading: ALiBi's linear bias makes the two sharp heads (slopes 1/4, 1/16) functions of the absolute gap size, and a head trained at mean gap 2 (P(gap=1) ~ 0.5) attends ~2x more broadly in tokens at test; Ruoss et al. 2023's gains came from encodings and tasks where only the ordering/relative range matters, and did not transfer to fixed-slope ALiBi at this scale. Expert iteration repaired most of it (2,400 AdamW steps at arange positions: round-4 solved 1127/1109/1161 vs 1157/1168/1191, metric_rl 1132 vs ~1172), so the -37 is mainly the weaker start compounding through fewer round-1/2 proofs (+467/+434/+574 vs 153's +1177 on seed 0). Steps 4260/4185/4159 (mean 4201 vs 4503, -6.7%; registered floor 4,200) look like a cost, but 149/160 saw ~8% pod-to-pod spread, so the randperm+sort cost is unmeasured. Positions are therefore not a free lever for 7-14-line transfer here; if anyone retries, keep gap 1 inside a local window (or leave the two sharp heads at arange) and stretch only the cross-line / mild-slope distances, and check held-out greedy on the bench first.",
